# bi-coin-iroha: parallel/abandoned Iroha implementation, not part of the thesis corpus
# (thesis scope is bi-coin-fabric on Hyperledger Fabric). Exclude the whole tree.
bi-coin-iroha/

# Graphify status is generated from the graph and must not feed back into its own corpus.
wiki/meta/graphify.md

# Generated output (never authored). Throwaway ledger clones: runtime-workspaces holds a
# full duplicate copy of chaincode/backend/network for every compliance run (~28k files).
bi-coin-fabric/benchmark/results/runtime-workspaces/

# Machine-generated Caliper/analysis artifacts. Authored evidence (REPORT.md, *.csv,
# metadata.json, manifests) at the top of each results dir is kept.
bi-coin-fabric/benchmark/results/*.html
bi-coin-fabric/benchmark/results/*/runs/
bi-coin-fabric/benchmark/results/*/source/

# Scratch working tree (contains a second full clone of the repo under workspace/).
tmp/

# Graphify's own rendered output - same reason as wiki/meta/graphify.md above.
graphify-out/graph.html
graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md

# Nested graphify output from earlier runs scoped to a subtree (chaincode/, backend/,
# frontend/ each have their own copy). Same reason as wiki/meta/graphify.md: a graph of
# the corpus must not ingest graphs of the corpus. Note the leading */ - graphify matches
# patterns per path component, so this catches nested copies WITHOUT excluding the
# top-level graphify-out/ that this run writes to.
*/graphify-out/

# Machine-generated statistical reports (scripts/analyze-benchmark-results.js).
# pilot6/REPORT.md alone is 13.5 MB / 92.5k rows of raw per-scenario tables;
# the cited numbers live in thesis/contents/chapter-4 and the .csv/.json sidecars.
bi-coin-fabric/benchmark/results/statistical-*/REPORT.md

# Vendored CTAN pgfplots distribution (untracked, unpacked release tree).
